What was the file path of the exploit used to get tier 0 access -
Evidence Found: An entry for expooo in the client column associated with the path /Users/irek/Desktop/expooo.
The Transparency, Consent, and Control (TCC) system manages app permissions. This database is a high-fidelity execution log; it records the absolute path of a binary at the moment it requests a sensitive permission, preserving the "original" location of malware even after it has been moved to the Trash.

/Users/irek/.Trash/.DS_Store
Evidence FOund: A record for expooo and switch_race.c within the Trash directory metadata.
Forensic Significance: These files store folder-specific viewing preferences. In the Trash, a .DS_Store file is vital because it stores "Put Back" metadata. This allows an investigator to determine the exact directory a file was originally deleted from.


